        // Since c.loans() public array generates a getter: function loans(uint256) returns (Loan). There's no direct length getter; use getLoan to avoid. Use c.getLoan in a safe way: but need loans length. Use try incremental probing: attempt to read index 0 to see existence.

        // We'll create a request and then try to clear it. First create a request via requestLoan.
        // requestLoan will call collateral().safeTransferFrom which will likely revert in many environments; therefore we must allow that clearRequest may revert. The property will relate the non-revert case.

