        // and that loan's request.active is false. We can observe loans via getLoan only if loans exist; we check existence by trying getLoan(clearLoanID)

        // Compute expected loan ID: if request creation succeeded and clear didn't revert, clearRequest pushes a loan at previous loans.length.
        // We cannot read previous loans length reliably if there were no loans; so instead we assert an invariant about the loan we just created if clear didn't revert: the loan's embedded request.active == false.

        // If clear didn't revert, then the caller (msg.sender which is this contract) became the lender (since clearRequest uses msg.sender as lender). We can read the loan via getLoan at index loansBefore (which is 0 if no prior loans). To obtain loansBefore robustly, probe indices until revert to find current length before operations is complex; instead we assert the logical property only using public getLoan for index 0 when clear didn't revert and when getLoan(0) succeeds.

        bool observableLoanExists = true;
        C.Loan memory loan0;
